Template: a3-core/configure-network
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Do you want to configure networking for a3-core?

Template: a3-core/install-default-network
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Install the standard default network configuration automatically?

Template: a3-core/interface
Type: string
Default: eno1
Description: Network interface to match (e.g. eno1)

Template: a3-core/address
Type: string
Default: 192.168.8.10/24
Description: Static IP address (CIDR), e.g. 192.168.8.10/24

Template: a3-core/gateway
Type: string
Default: 192.168.8.1
Description: Gateway address

Template: a3-core/dns
Type: string
Default: 192.168.8.1
Description: DNS server address

Template: a3-core/headless-display
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Draw to a dummy screen instead of a monitor?
 Only for a Core that runs without a monitor and is used over VNC. X then
 draws to a virtual 1920x1080 screen, and a monitor that is plugged in stays
 black. Answer no on a machine with a screen, such as one that also runs
 A3 Motion with its touch panel.

Template: a3-core/audio-port
Type: string
Default:
Description: Second network socket for AES67 audio and PTP (empty: none)
 The second socket carries the audio network: AES67 streams and the PTP clock,
 on a subnet of their own without gateway, so the Core's own network on the
 first socket stays as it is. Name that socket here (for example enp5s0), or
 leave it empty to use one socket only. Takes effect at the next boot.

Template: a3-core/audio-address
Type: string
Default: 192.168.9.10/24
Description: This Core's address on the audio network (CIDR)
 Its own subnet, different from the first socket's: a reply always leaves by
 the socket it came in on. No gateway and no DNS on this network.

Template: a3-core/replace-config
Type: multiselect
Choices-C: ${choices_c}
Choices: ${choices}
Description: Local files differ from this package. Which should be replaced?
 These parts of ~/.config differ from what this package ships -- left over
 from an older a3, or edited on this machine. A chosen part is replaced; every
 file that is replaced is kept first in ~/.config/a3-replaced/<time>/ and
 named on the output. A part that is not chosen stays as it is.

Template: a3-core/preseeded
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: for internal use
 Set by the a3-system installer together with its network answers, so the
 postinst takes them without asking. Cleared by the postinst on every install.

Template: a3-core/ssh-key
Type: string
Default:
Description: Public ssh key allowed to log in as aaa (empty: none)
 Paste one public key line, for example "ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@laptop".
 It is added to ~/.ssh/authorized_keys of the user aaa, next to the keys
 already there, and is not added twice. Leave it empty to add nothing. The
 answer is forgotten after the install, so a later upgrade does not put back
 a key that was removed by hand.
